bus.pack_settings.command_impulse=\n§l§6Command Permission Level§r\nSets the command’s default Minecraft permission level. This determines which players can see and use the command.\n\nThis is the§l base permission level§r only. Bedrock Utility Suite may apply additional role-specific permissions or restrictions on top of the setting.\n\nFor example, setting a command to Admin allows Admin-level players to access it by default, while BUS role settings can further restrict or configure access.\n\nDisabled — prevents the command from being registered entirely.\nEveryone — allows the command to be ran from anywhere, even by non-operators.\nGameDirectors — restricts the command to operators (including command blocks).\nAdmin — restricts the command to operators (excluding command blocks).\nHost — restricts the command to the player hosting the world.\nOwner — restricts the command to the server console.\n\nImpulse Command Permission Level
